Z||000000||MontanaFiero||10-03-2001||04:26 AM||||Got my 86 SE driveable, with its fairly fresh 3.4 Liter Camaro motor. This motor only has 9,000 miles on it. When I took the car for a drive today for the first time, I thought my speedometer was broken. Hell, when I started out (first gear) I glanced down at the speedo and it said 35. The next time I did that I noticed that I was passing cars and realized I was just getting to 35 faster than I was used to. <P>Boy am I gonna get myself into trouble with this thing!!!<P>------------------<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://members.home.net/blee291/fiero/mtfieroplate.jpg"> ||||reg||11
Z||000001||kempo||10-03-2001||01:30 PM||||Boy I can't wait to install my 3.4L!!  I've got it, but I'm waiting for my 2.8 to die (which I am beginning to wonder if it will, it is about to roll 135,000).  How much time did your swap take you?  And where did you get your engine?  <BR>Good luck with your newly found toy =)||||reg||1
Z||000002||MontanaFiero||10-03-2001||03:47 PM||||$1000 for the motor, then somewhere along the line I managed to dump another grand into it. I don't know how long it took, it seemed way too long, though, but the job was relatively easy. I got the motor out of a local wrecking yard. It had been sitting up on a shelf since about '94. The '93 camaro it was in was wrecked only after 9,000 miles were put on it, so I have a very tight motor.<P>P.S.  I am running Mobil 1 along with GM RapidFire spark plugs if anyone was interested.<P>------------------<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://members.home.net/blee291/fiero/mtfieroplate.jpg"> ||||reg||1
